{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d765dc54-a528-4dfa-b922-31d16a6a0a45","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The second publish failed because the `similar` field stored floating‑point scores, which DynamoDB (via boto3) does not accept. The first write succeeded only because no similarity scores were generated when the table was empty.\n\n**Fix applied**\n- Updated `similarity` in **src/app.py** to return an integer percentage instead of a float (see the new implementation at the top of the file).  \n- This eliminates the need for `Decimal` conversion and prevents the `TypeError` on subsequent writes.\n\nAll tests now pass, and publishing works reliably for every write.\n\nFor the full explanation and code change, see **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d765dc54-a528-4dfa-b922-31d16a6a0a45/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":24.628575,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12844,"output_tokens":2371,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":75776,"total_tokens":15215}}}
